 "title": "Ошибочная бутылка  (The Wrong Bottle)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Senya is ill, and Max suspects the bar's fake cognac is to blame. At the same moment Barinov asks Kostya for a bottle of cognac, and Kostya hands him exactly the wrong one. Keep an eye on which bottle ends up on the table.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Костя, это просто ужас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сеня отравился нашим коньяком.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О нет, что делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Костя, дай мне бутылку коньяка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ту, которая стоит справа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вот эту бутылку?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нет, дай мне другую. Да, эту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф забрал наш коньяк!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо забрать эту бутылку назад.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я не могу к нему подойти.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай, Костя, ты должен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я пойду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the bottle mix-up, slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Костя, это просто ужас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Kostya, this is just awful!' \"Uzhas\", horror, is the everyday way to say something is awful.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сеня отравился нашим коньяком.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya's been poisoned by our cognac.' \"Otravilsya\" ends in \"-sya\": 'poisoned himself'. The cause takes the 'by' ending: \"nashim konyakom\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О нет, что делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh no, what do we do?' \"Chto delat?\", 'what to do?', needs no 'we' at all. It's also the title of a famous Russian novel.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Костя, дай мне бутылку коньяка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Kostya, give me a bottle of cognac.' \"Day\", give!, is the friendly form. No 'of' needed: \"butylku konyaka\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ту, которая стоит справа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The one on the right.' In Russian a bottle stands, \"stoit\", rather than sits. \"Sprava\", on the right.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вот эту бутылку?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This bottle here?' \"Vot\" points: here it is. \"Butylka\" becomes \"butylku\" as the thing handed over.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нет, дай мне другую. Да, эту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, give me another. Yes, that one.' \"Druguyu\", another, ends the same way as \"butylku\", the bottle it stands for.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф забрал наш коньяк!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef's taken our cognac!' \"Zabral\", took away: the \"za-\" means he took it for himself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо забрать эту бутылку назад.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We need to get this bottle back.' \"Nazad\", back, finishes the line. \"Nado zabrat\", 'needed to take away'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я не могу к нему подойти.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I can't just walk up to him.' \"Podoyti\", to go up to: \"pod-\" means up close. After \"k\", to, \"emu\" becomes \"nemu\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай, Костя, ты должен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come on, Kostya, you have to.' \"Davay\", literally 'give', is the Russian 'come on'. \"Dolzhen\", must, is the form for a man.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я пойду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, I'll go.' \"Poydu\", I'll go, on foot. \"Khorosho\" here just means okay. Here it is again, mix-up and all.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Костя, это просто ужас!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сеня отравился нашим коньяком.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О нет, что делать?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Костя, дай мне бутылку коньяка.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ту, которая стоит справа.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вот эту бутылку?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нет, дай мне другую. Да, эту.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф забрал наш коньяк!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо забрать эту бутылку назад.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я не могу к нему подойти.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай, Костя, ты должен.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я пойду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Kostya has to get a bottle back from the chef's table, which is easier said than done. Remember that in Russian a bottle stands: \"butylka stoit\". See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
